 2hCFwK8TKn47\n\nJoin us for an afternoon of poetry on the porch\, in celeb
 ration of Creative Writing lecturers Stephanie Horvath and Hieu Minh Nguye
 n\, as they launch their newest poetry collections Field of Vision and Sta
 ying Still.\n\nThis event is open to Stanford affiliates and the general p
 ublic. Refreshments provided and books available for purchase. Registratio
 n is encouraged but not required\; register here.\n\n____\n\nIn Horvath's 
 Field of Vision\, we traverse the thresholds of past and future\, reality 
 and dream\, as we accompany the speaker through deserts\, forests\, rivers
 \, and coasts. These poems capture\, viscerally and intimately\, a sense o
 f deep time in the rural landscape—dark\, damp dirt on one’s hands\, a
  desert over which vultures circle\, the decay of wet leaves on a forest f
 loor. A meditation on the horror and resplendence of nature\, Field of Vis
 ion invokes the ancient history that weaves into each of our individual hi
 stories—the earth\, the animals\, the fossils\, the primordial echoes th
 at shape us all.\n\nThe highly anticipated follow-up to the award-winning 
 poetry collection Not Here\, Nguyen’s Staying Still centers on the quest
 ion of how: How do our anxieties around the idea of belonging estrange us 
 from the very world we seek to belong in? How impossible does it feel to s
 tay still and face ourselves? From the intimate longing of queer boyhood t
 o the collective expectations imposed upon children of refugees\, these po
 ems face head-on the rejections\, grief\, and violence we fear in fracture
